WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.169 --> 00:00:01.523
- Good morning, Believe Nation,

00:00:01.523 --> 00:00:04.728
today's message is push more!

00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:06.602
Over to you, Jennifer Aniston.

00:00:06.602 --> 00:00:08.923
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.923 --> 00:00:11.415
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.415 --> 00:00:14.242
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:18.443
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.443 --> 00:00:20.775
- I was saying the other day to somebody,

00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:23.608
I think all actors who are, maybe,

00:00:24.795 --> 00:00:28.712
gratefully are successful,
sometimes if you are

00:00:29.932 --> 00:00:32.662
identified with something like Friends,

00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:34.809
you almost feel like you're
an actor in a closet,

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:38.557
always trying, like, I want to
do more, you know what I mean?

00:00:38.557 --> 00:00:41.751
And it's always, there's
always a little bit

00:00:41.751 --> 00:00:43.896
of a struggle and a challenge.

00:00:43.896 --> 00:00:47.228
But I find that exciting,
you know what I mean?

00:00:47.228 --> 00:00:51.728
To keep pushing myself and
to keep challenging myself

00:00:51.728 --> 00:00:53.800
and taking risks, I think it's important

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.300
not to get lazy and stay safe.

00:00:57.435 --> 00:00:58.739
- This is a really important message,

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:01.368
and one that entrepreneurs
really struggle with,

00:01:01.368 --> 00:01:03.779
because when you don't have a boss,

00:01:03.779 --> 00:01:06.585
it's really hard to push
yourself to do more.

00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:09.616
Entrepreneurs struggle
with pushing themselves

00:01:09.616 --> 00:01:10.809
out of their comfort zone because

00:01:10.809 --> 00:01:12.093
there's nobody to report to!

00:01:12.093 --> 00:01:13.891
And yes, we report to our customers,

00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:15.724
if we're under a deadline, or a customer

00:01:15.724 --> 00:01:17.567
wants to get this thing
done by a certain time

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:20.059
and you're pushing yourself
hard, you're crushing it

00:01:20.059 --> 00:01:22.369
to go out and get that thing done on time,

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:25.348
but if your customer
isn't pushing you hard,

00:01:25.348 --> 00:01:27.523
then it's easy to be a little bit lazy!

00:01:27.523 --> 00:01:29.718
Not that you're going to sleep in all day,

00:01:29.718 --> 00:01:31.840
but you're not pushing yourself

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.003
to be the best that you can be.

00:01:34.003 --> 00:01:36.375
You maybe taking a little
extra long at lunch,

00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:38.197
you may be coming a
little late to the office,

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.600
you're going to be spending more time

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.905
just browsing around on social media,

00:01:41.905 --> 00:01:46.638
or just being a little bit of
a slacker than you should be,

00:01:46.638 --> 00:01:48.588
because there's nobody to kick your butt.

00:01:48.588 --> 00:01:50.611
There's nobody to say, "Let's do this,"

00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:52.605
because when you commit to somebody else,

00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:54.497
you're much more likely to follow through.

00:01:54.497 --> 00:01:56.476
And when there's nobody
for you to commit to,

00:01:56.476 --> 00:01:59.187
as entrepreneurs, we are our own boss,

00:01:59.187 --> 00:02:02.519
there's nobody we're committing
to besides ourselves,

00:02:02.519 --> 00:02:05.253
we're going to let ourselves down a lot.

00:02:05.253 --> 00:02:08.081
And so I think the capacity
and the willingness

00:02:08.081 --> 00:02:11.255
to push yourself consistently, hard,

00:02:11.255 --> 00:02:13.274
makes the difference
between a really successful

00:02:13.274 --> 00:02:15.904
entrepreneur, and just
an average, mediocre one.

00:02:15.904 --> 00:02:18.304
And so how do you push yourself harder

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.025
when you are an entrepreneur?

00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:23.148
A couple ideas, one, have important goals.

00:02:23.148 --> 00:02:26.264
Have goals that you look
at consistently, daily,

00:02:26.264 --> 00:02:27.971
that are big goals, that are meaningful,

00:02:27.971 --> 00:02:29.307
that are important to you, remind yourself

00:02:29.307 --> 00:02:31.640
why you're doing this, to
get the energy to get up

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.876
and want to push harder every day.

00:02:33.876 --> 00:02:36.194
Two, have somebody to kick your butt.

00:02:36.194 --> 00:02:38.845
Whether it's a mastermind
group, whether it's an adviser,

00:02:38.845 --> 00:02:40.692
whether it's an online group, something,

00:02:40.692 --> 00:02:42.761
somebody that you're committing to to say,

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:44.434
I'm going to get this thing done.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:47.021
I have a mass friend group
that we meet every month,

00:02:47.021 --> 00:02:48.598
and in between, you
have a weekly phone call

00:02:48.598 --> 00:02:52.332
with somebody in your team,
and you're pushing each other.

00:02:52.332 --> 00:02:54.681
Because if you come to that
next meeting the next month

00:02:54.681 --> 00:02:56.981
and you didn't do what you
say you were going to do,

00:02:56.981 --> 00:02:59.267
the group starts holding a
little bit of flame to your foot,

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:01.242
say like, "What's going on?

00:03:01.242 --> 00:03:02.550
"You've been saying that
you're going to do this

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:05.214
"but you haven't, come
on, let's get in shape."

00:03:05.214 --> 00:03:06.548
You don't want to come to that meeting

00:03:06.548 --> 00:03:08.073
and not have done the things that you said

00:03:08.073 --> 00:03:11.127
you were going to do, and
so that accountability

00:03:11.127 --> 00:03:13.321
is really important for entrepreneurs.

00:03:13.321 --> 00:03:16.830
And then three, we talked
about it a ton on this channel,

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.727
the environment and the routine.

00:03:18.727 --> 00:03:21.644
It's so easy to get up for one day.

00:03:22.921 --> 00:03:24.997
It's hard to get up consistently,

00:03:24.997 --> 00:03:27.303
it's hard to keep that energy level high,

00:03:27.303 --> 00:03:30.827
and so, build whatever
gets you pumped and excited

00:03:30.827 --> 00:03:33.372
into your morning routine consistently.

00:03:33.372 --> 00:03:34.572
So whatever you start your day with,

00:03:34.572 --> 00:03:36.151
think about what makes you come alive,

00:03:36.151 --> 00:03:38.539
again, if it's watching a
video, or reading a book,

00:03:38.539 --> 00:03:40.690
or viewing your goals, or
listening to some music,

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.928
whatever it is.

00:03:41.928 --> 00:03:44.402
For me, it's being around
famous entrepreneurs,

00:03:44.402 --> 00:03:46.750
successful people, and
seeing what they're doing.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.722
Yes, their strategies helped
me, that's part of it,

00:03:49.722 --> 00:03:52.053
but a big part of it's just
seeing people going off

00:03:52.053 --> 00:03:55.576
doing amazing things, makes
me want to push myself harder.

00:03:55.576 --> 00:03:58.187
They push me to do more,
because the people around me

00:03:58.187 --> 00:03:59.894
aren't really pushing me to do more.

00:03:59.894 --> 00:04:01.954
And so whatever gets you excited,

00:04:01.954 --> 00:04:04.059
whatever makes you feel
like you want to push

00:04:04.059 --> 00:04:08.202
a little bit harder, build
that into your daily routine

00:04:08.202 --> 00:04:10.247
as opposed to having it randomly happen

00:04:10.247 --> 00:04:12.466
because you turned on
YouTube at four o'clock

00:04:12.466 --> 00:04:14.139
in the afternoon.

00:04:14.139 --> 00:04:18.447
Build it in, every day, so
you're pushing yourself harder.

00:04:18.447 --> 00:04:19.871
So the question of the day today is,

00:04:19.871 --> 00:04:21.420
how do you push yourself?

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.165
How do you keep yourself accountable

00:04:23.165 --> 00:04:25.739
to doing the things that
you say you're going to do,

00:04:25.739 --> 00:04:28.435
and reaching your actual potential?

00:04:28.435 --> 00:04:30.448
What do you, leave it
in the comments below,

00:04:30.448 --> 00:04:32.098
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:04:32.098 --> 00:04:34.527
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Cathy Cashmere

00:04:34.527 --> 00:04:37.856
from cccinspire.com,
Cathy, thank you so much

00:04:37.856 --> 00:04:40.201
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word,

00:04:40.201 --> 00:04:41.863
it really, really,
really means a lot to me

00:04:41.863 --> 00:04:43.328
and I hope you enjoyed it.

00:04:43.328 --> 00:04:45.719
Thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you,

00:04:45.719 --> 00:04:47.852
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:47.852 --> 00:04:50.002
and whatever your one word is,

00:04:50.002 --> 00:04:52.360
much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.868
for another shot of entspresso.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:57.399
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:57.399 --> 00:05:01.331
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:01.331 --> 00:05:02.442
- Hey Believe Nation, for those of you

00:05:02.442 --> 00:05:05.213
who want a little more content
on pushing yourself harder,

00:05:05.213 --> 00:05:08.270
I think you'll enjoy
